    LLM: 'Game: Bonanza Pai Gow. Chinese Pai Gow variant with 3 bets: Main (traditional), Bonus (hand strength payout), Tie (push payout). 32 Chinese domino tiles. 4 tiles â†’ split into High/Low hands. Main bet optional. Bonus hits every 3.7 hands. Crown Casino Melbourne 2001.',
    Player: 'You have 4 tiles. Your best High Hand using two strong tiles ranks well, but your Low Hand would be weak. Alternatively, you could balance both hands to improve your push (Tie bet) chances. You have bets on Main AND Tie. How do you split?',
    objective: "Form two hands (high hand and low hand) from your 4 tiles that both beat the Banker's corresponding hands.",
    gameplay: 'Each player receives 4 tiles and must split them into a High Hand (2 tiles) and a Low Hand (2 tiles). The High Hand must rank at least equal to the Low Hand according to standard Pai Gow tile rankings. After all players have set their hands, the Banker reveals their 4 tiles and forms their high and low hands.',
